# NOTE: this full-suite attempt was killed by the validation timeout after 13 inline cases
# on a loaded shared host (a concurrent gate agent was running host suites). It proves
# nothing; teardown-targeted.log is the evidence for the four cases this change touches.
ok - teardown leaves opencode's busy plugin in the returned pool worktree as on main
ok - hidden untracked work is refused before return while a clean control returns
ok - content fallback distinguishes unavailable Git proof, containment, conflicts, and unlanded content
ok - status archival is opt-in and preserves the complete log
ok - config-absent teardown does not read or invoke record export
ok - unopted teardown ignores symlinked config when record export is absent
ok - teardown commits the record archive before deleting sources and fails closed when export cannot commit
ok - forced secondmate teardown exports task records from the child sub-state
ok - record export waits for endpoint quiescence and retry captures records changed after refusal
ok - forced secondmate retirement preserves two descendant levels and refuses linked child directories
ok - local missing-status retirement stays lock-free without creating an archive
ok - reused task IDs never overwrite archives and retention removes only old owned logs
ok - archive sources and directories reject symlinks; pruning never follows children links
